WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.840
Welcome to our training on how to set up a coupon.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:06.640
You can set up coupons from the Coupons dashboard in Seller Central.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.760
To access the Coupons dashboard, one, sign in to your Seller Central account.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.320
Two, click the menu icon in the top left corner of Seller Central.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.640
Three, hover over the advertising section and select coupons.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.503
Four, if this is your first time setting up a coupon, you'll arrive at a page providing more information

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:27.120
about them.

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.880
Review it and then click the create your first coupon button.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:36.000
If you've set up a coupon before, you'll arrive at your Coupons dashboard automatically.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.400
You'll see any coupons you've already submitted and can filter them by status.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.280
This is also where you'll edit or deactivate your coupons,

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.577
but keep in mind that you can't make these changes within approximately six hours of a coupon's

00:00:48.577 --> 00:00:49.200
start time.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:53.840
We use this time to make sure your coupon offers value to Amazon customers.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.480
Follow these steps to create your coupon.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:59.760
One, click the create a new coupon button.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.840
Two, search for a product by its stockkeeping unit or SKU.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.960
You can also search for it by its Amazon standard identification number or ASIN.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.240
Three, click go and select add to coupon.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.360
You can add up to 200 ASINs to your coupon.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:21.455
If you're adding more than just a few, stop here and use the create in bulk button on your Coupons

00:01:21.455 --> 00:01:21.760
dashboard.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.720
Rather than adding ASINs one by one, you can upload a spreadsheet with your product information

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.280
to add them to your coupon all at once.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.920
If you're adding ASINs individually, search by ASIN or product title to manage

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.640
which products and variations appear on your coupon.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.920
Four, select continue to next step.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.080
Five, choose whether you'll be creating a percentage off or money off coupon

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:47.520
and enter the discount amount you'd like to offer your customers.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.360
For more expensive items, we recommend using a money off coupon.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.600
Customers will be able to quickly reference exactly how much they'll be saving

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.080
without having to calculate their discount.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.960
Whether you choose percentage off or money off, however,

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.800
we recommend creating a coupon that discounts the product by at least 10%.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.960
Six, choose whether you'll allow customers to redeem your coupon once or multiple times.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.560
Seven, enter your budget, which isn't a hard limit and should be used for planning purposes only.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.851
Eight, select continue to next step.

00:02:19.851 --> 00:02:23.280
Nine, click title guidelines to review our rules

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.880
and then enter your coupon title.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:30.160
Customers will see this title under the coupon image while they browse the coupon's home page.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.360
We automatically generate the first three words that appear on each of your coupons

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.360
based on the discount you entered.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.760
All you have to do is let your customers know what products the savings will apply to.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.360
Ten, choose which Amazon customer type will be eligible to use your coupon.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:51.440
You can make it available to all customers or only Amazon Prime,

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.160
Amazon Student or Amazon Family Members.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:00.720
Eleven, schedule the duration of your coupon and keep in mind that all coupons expire after 90 days.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:05.040
To start, we recommend setting a duration of two to three months.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.160
Twelve, select continue to next step.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.760
Thirteen, review your coupon details.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.800
If you notice any errors,

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:18.160
select the numbered circle related to that step to go back and make any necessary updates.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.738
Fourteen, click submit coupon.

00:03:20.738 --> 00:03:22.960
If your coupon is approved,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:27.200
customers will discover it in search results on product detail pages

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:30.160
and on the coupon's home page in the Amazon store.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.680
This concludes our training on how to set up a coupon.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.880
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
